#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9fa087f-f6db-5d41-bce6-176e0dfc84bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265643} {:answer/id #uuid "8291aef2-a55a-5035-960c-b2fd32db51b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265644} {:answer/id #uuid "74e0f6fd-d7a9-5e32-b935-3d2d63d15eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265645} {:answer/id #uuid "16abd149-1622-5870-acac-08550572af4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265646} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e71bada-abf2-5012-a4dd-26de4973c091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265642}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d2067af-e1b2-5f04-ba26-5b2307cb8aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-120017" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d81ed476-a3a2-57be-b7f0-4b2de132956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265650} {:answer/id #uuid "b553aac5-8d44-507e-85e2-483a7ca6ee2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265651} {:answer/id #uuid "08fbb1fa-cd53-52b6-8196-cc14538e4a8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265652} {:answer/id #uuid "820c3579-99cc-58ec-ad98-1a63743b7c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265653} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe005c4-cf2b-5111-832b-c7b6225601ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81ed476-a3a2-57be-b7f0-4b2de132956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265650} :answer-field/id #uuid "b47f6277-8c45-5320-8eb8-6b1acce1b2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265649}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "641c1e03-d0a1-58b9-b0a0-52b1bb02a882" :question/math-academy-id "q-120020" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "876f3cb0-9875-5c76-ac3c-e16da162deb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265657} {:answer/id #uuid "2bbbd93d-1010-56a9-8693-f0f6a844bdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265658} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ca4ed2-5a3d-503c-b2a5-2ca6dacd51b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265659} {:answer/id #uuid "111a3ffd-2cb7-50cf-8617-b520d655dcef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265660} {:answer/id #uuid "ef87a0b6-edd6-54f8-8a5c-df4fb24cd609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef87a0b6-edd6-54f8-8a5c-df4fb24cd609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265661} :answer-field/id #uuid "deaaab4d-877d-581d-919e-874dd9691d2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fbc5ec2-c0cd-5828-8f6b-007deeaf2dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-120032" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =4(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{210}^{∘} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a1b441f-384a-5e42-aeed-0aaf3c68cc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265664} {:answer/id #uuid "972dbc60-7240-5537-b0d6-f02ca27e8b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265665} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f24a28-638a-59a0-988f-f7c57b26e03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265666} {:answer/id #uuid "d59e8d2c-2463-5569-aa2e-f72d48fb3da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265667} {:answer/id #uuid "7fffe3ac-c891-58ea-a3f5-0ee000d966fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fffe3ac-c891-58ea-a3f5-0ee000d966fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265668} :answer-field/id #uuid "e005343d-19aa-5fec-adba-ffe1d0a55ff1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265663}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1938b105-5884-5db6-9c07-161191c66b44" :question/math-academy-id "q-24650" :question/problem "$8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}) & =4\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d784ba57-32cf-5475-9502-09c02e951bf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265671} {:answer/id #uuid "6b03fa01-a870-518a-acd6-0ce651777f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265672} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b24666-1aca-5be9-819d-d91bfb268761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265673} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9b41f1-3aa5-5cc6-ab51-cbf27da442df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265674} {:answer/id #uuid "50348e45-9894-5c3b-b3d4-2a6bf83a31d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b03fa01-a870-518a-acd6-0ce651777f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265672} :answer-field/id #uuid "b233644c-03af-50a1-bd84-6cd086cd0de8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265670}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "610433dc-861c-5a73-95c1-d209a03b7b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-24792" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
